# Corporate root CA certs are gitignored by default.
#
# A root CA is a public key, not a secret, so committing one to share with your
# team is usually fine — but that should be a deliberate act, not an accident.
# To commit yours:
#
#   git add -f snyk-ads/files/home/corp-ca/zscaler-root-ca.crt
#
snyk-ads/files/home/corp-ca/*.crt
!snyk-ads/files/home/corp-ca/*.crt.example

# Never commit these. The ADS push key is a live credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local scratch
*.bak
*.bak.yaml
*.log
